// C11 6.8.3: an expression statement is an expression followed by `;`.
// madc's expression engine stops BEFORE a closer and no statement parser
// checked for its `;`, so `x = 3 }` ran (exit 3). The statement now pays
// its terminator (Program::require_statement_terminator).
// Oracle: gcc "error: expected ';' before '}' token", clang "error:
// expected ';' after expression".
int main(void) { int x; x = 3 }
